WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.278
Welcome. This is your ten-day plan for letter sounds that will not stick.

2
00:00:04.728 --> 00:00:07.556
It is about eight sounds. These eight, in this order.

3
00:00:13.756 --> 00:00:14.622
As in nest.

4
00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:16.976
As in moon.

5
00:00:18.595 --> 00:00:25.734
The goal is that your child says all eight, in any order, a day after the last lesson, and reads short new words with them.

6
00:00:26.234 --> 00:00:31.735
That is the goal. It is not a promise. Day ten is a check, and it tells you what to do next.

7
00:00:32.535 --> 00:00:36.262
This plan is for a child who does not know the letter sounds yet.

8
00:00:36.712 --> 00:00:40.097
Or who says the names of the letters when you ask for the sounds.

9
00:00:40.547 --> 00:00:43.966
Or who learns a sound today, and has lost it by tomorrow.

10
00:00:44.416 --> 00:00:50.773
Losing sounds overnight is common at four, five and six. It is not a sign that something is wrong.

11
00:00:51.573 --> 00:00:57.932
Why only eight, and not the whole alphabet? Because a few sounds that stay are worth more than many that do not.

12
00:00:58.382 --> 00:01:02.631
And with these eight, a child can already read real words. Like this one.

13
00:01:05.790 --> 00:01:06.752
The word is sat.

14
00:01:07.652 --> 00:01:14.110
The ten days also show you the way of working. After that you carry on the same way with the other letters.

15
00:01:14.910 --> 00:01:19.415
Here is what is inside. Ten days. One page a day, about ten minutes.

16
00:01:19.865 --> 00:01:25.013
Day one is a short check. It shows you where to start. Day ten shows you what has stayed.

17
00:01:25.463 --> 00:01:30.720
Every day has a short video like this one, for you. It shows you what to do before you do it.

18
00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:38.172
And under the videos are the eight letters. Tap one, and you hear its real sound. Use it whenever you are not sure.

19
00:01:38.972 --> 00:01:42.628
Here is what makes a sound stay. Two new sounds a day, at most.

20
00:01:43.078 --> 00:01:50.324
Every day starts with every old sound. On the page it is a strip called Bring back. It is the one part you never skip.

21
00:01:50.774 --> 00:01:56.130
Each sound has one picture word and one small hand action. They are hooks for the memory.

22
00:01:56.580 --> 00:02:00.387
Here they all are, on one page. Keep it where your child can see it.

23
00:02:00.837 --> 00:02:06.973
And from day six, your child uses the sounds to read small words. Then the sounds have a purpose.

24
00:02:07.773 --> 00:02:14.074
This plan uses small letters only. It does not teach capital letters, and it does not teach handwriting.

25
00:02:14.874 --> 00:02:21.361
Here is how each day works. First, watch that day's video. Scan the code on the page with your phone.

26
00:02:21.811 --> 00:02:26.379
Then read the yellow box at the top of the page. It gives you three short steps.

27
00:02:26.829 --> 00:02:29.977
Do the first job together. That takes about two minutes.

28
00:02:30.427 --> 00:02:34.569
Then your child carries on with the page, and shows you a few things at the end.

29
00:02:35.019 --> 00:02:39.898
On three of the days there is a sound track for your child. You press play and step away.

30
00:02:40.698 --> 00:02:43.759
You need the printed pages, a pencil, and crayons.

31
00:02:44.209 --> 00:02:49.420
When you are ready, start with day one. It is a short check, and it takes about three minutes.
